@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: make `proveo init` the ONE place a credential is provisioned, and retire env-carried keys behind it — proposed 2026-09-15
' OPEN WORK. The credential STAGE shipped 2026-09-16; everything remaining in
' this file did not. No `covers:` lines: _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the
' SPEC-reference rule, what shipped is covered by the two wireframes below, and
' a plan claiming shipped files makes the drift guard fire twice for one change.
'   what SHIPPED, and where it is drawn:
'     _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-wireframe.puml  the list and its fields
'     _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-entry.puml      the field rules + verify
'   the decision this implements ... _spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml
'   where a secret rests ........... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml
'   the file this would retire ..... _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml
'   who injects on sbx today ....... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   what the agent may hold ........ _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'   the gate that decides a service  _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml
'   the code the OPEN work touches:
'     internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (agentCredentials, Spec) — the ownAgent
'       gate below, which is the whole of the unbuilt half
'     internal/run/run.go (resolveCredentials, StoreHeld) — where P2's precedence
'       would go, and where nothing decides one today
'     internal/sbx/secret.go (SecretSetArgs), internal/sbx/run.go (StoredSecretNames)
'
' ── THE STAGE SHIPPED; THIS FILE IS THE REST ───────────────────────────────
' `cmd/proveo/init_credentials.go` landed 2026-09-16 (9a3c724, then db1cd83 and
' 3679ce3). What it DRAWS is specified in the two wireframes named above; what it
' did to the code is in git. A plan is a poor place to keep a changelog, so the
' detail that lived here is gone and only the consequence stays:
'
'   proveo now OFFERS a credential surface and GATES NOTHING on it. A run with no
'   credential proceeds — the agent comes up at its own login, `/login` is the
'   AGENT's command, and 3679ce3 reduced the whole routes block to one line:
'   "<name> is starting without a credential — run `proveo init` to persist
'   credentials between runs". `SandboxAuthRoutes`, `PrintSubscriptionAuthHints`
'   and `SandboxAuthRefusal` are deleted, and internal/run/run_test.go fails if
'   any of the three returns.
'
'   So an operator can now PUT a credential where proveo will find it, and the
'   broker path still cannot USE it on sbx. Everything below is that gap.
'
' ── THE OPEN WORK, AND NONE OF IT IS MADE LIKELIER BY THE STAGE LANDING ────
'   P2 PREFERRED  a store entry does NOT yet outrank the env var of the same
'                 provider, and the run header does not say which won.
'   P3 WARNED     a workspace-.env-only key is not warned with the move command;
'                 _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml does not retire yet.
'   P4 REFUSED    `forward` still accepts a plaintext key for every provider.
'   MIXIN-KIT BROKERING, which this plan says must come FIRST and which the
'                 stage does not touch: `Spec()` still calls `agentCredentials`
'                 only under `if ownAgent`, so `--credentials broker` remains a
'                 NO-OP on sbx for every def but cecli. The three broker 401s
'                 stand. A provisioned store does not fix them — the naming was
'                 measured necessary and INSUFFICIENT, and nothing in 9a3c724
'                 declares a credential for a mixin kit.
'
' ── THE PROPOSAL, IN THE OPERATOR'S WORDS ──────────────────────────────────
' "Focus on `proveo init`, running it allows the user to set all their
' credentials safely. Either login to subscriptions, input API keys."
'
' host-held-provider-keys.puml decided on 2026-09-09 that plaintext keys leave
' every env surface. It did not name the surface that REPLACES them. This plan
' names it: `proveo init`, the command an operator already runs once per host.
'
' ── WHY NOW: THE SUITE FOUND SOMETHING BIGGER THAN THE NAMING TASK ─────────
' host-held-provider-keys.puml B2 reads "MAP, DON'T RENAME … add a slug map and
' show both names. NO LONGER A BLOCKER — it is a task." The task was not done,
' and on 2026-09-15 the e2e suite measured what it costs. One run, one key:
'
'   OPENCODE_API_KEY  --credentials forward  POST /zen/v1/chat/completions  200
'   OPENCODE_API_KEY  --credentials broker   same endpoint, same key        401
'   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY --credentials broker   same shape, other provider     401
'
' The credential is good — forward spends it. The two halves of the store
' disagree about what it is CALLED:
'
'   proveo WRITES   sbx.SecretSet(kv[0], …) where kv[0] is the ENV VAR name,
'                   and the run prints "sandbox secret: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY".
'   proveo READS    agentCredentials gates on stored[name] where name is the
'                   SERVICE id from provider.Detect — "anthropic".
'
' `sbx secret ls` on the host that produced the 401s holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
' OPENCODE_API_KEY, CURSOR_API_KEY … beside two service-shaped entries, cursor
' and github. So stored["anthropic"] is false, the KitCredential is never
' declared, the proxy attaches nothing, and the provider answers 401. Nothing
' is broken in the proxy: it was never asked to manage a credential.
'
' The test that would have caught this exists — TestSandboxKitProxyManagesThe-
' Credential — and skips behind PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1, so it has never run in a
' normal suite. An opt-in test guarding a decided-but-unbuilt task is a gap
' that reports as green.
'
' ── THE NAMING THEORY WAS TESTED AND REFUTED, SAME DAY ─────────────────────
' `sbx secret set --force opencode` was given the SAME key that forward spends
' successfully. `sbx secret ls` then showed `opencode (stored)` — so an
' arbitrary name IS storable; sbx's "available services" list is the set it has
' built-in knowledge for, not a whitelist, and the store already held six
' env-var-named entries proving it. TestOpenCodeAuth/zen re-run:
'
'   forward  200      broker  401      unchanged
'
' So the mismatch is real and is NOT what produces the 401. The rendered kit
' says why. `proveo run opencode --credentials broker --print` writes
' <state>/egress/<sid>/sbx/kit/spec.yaml, and that file is 41 lines of
' `kind: mixin` with permissions, environment and setup — and NO `credentials:`
' block.
'
' ── THE REAL CAUSE: BROKERING IS OWN-AGENT ONLY ────────────────────────────
' Spec() calls agentCredentials ONLY under `if ownAgent`, and
' `ownAgent := !in.Shell && sbx.DeclaresOwnAgent(harness)`, which is
' `BuiltinAgent(target) == "" && AgentKitEnabled()`. Every proveo def except
' cecli maps to a built-in sbx agent — claudecode→claude, opencode→opencode,
' cursor→cursor, codex→codex — so DeclaresOwnAgent is false, the kit stays a
' mixin, and no KitCredential is ever declared for it.
'
' On the sandbox backend `--credentials broker` is therefore a NO-OP for every
' def but one, while the run header still prints "broker: 5 providers injected
' at the egress layer (anthropic, openai, xai, google, opencode)". That line is
' true of the docker rendering, where an egress sidecar does the injecting. It
' is false under sbx, and it is the reason three tests report a credential
' failure that is really a missing feature.
'
' The naming scheme below is still required — a declared credential has to name
' a service the store can answer for — but it is the SECOND half of the fix.
' The first half is declaring credentials for mixin-kit defs.
'
' ── WHAT INIT WOULD DO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A fourth stage, after the readiness checks that already run:
'
'   1 ENUMERATE  every provider proveo knows, from the same registry the run
'                path uses, so the list cannot drift from what a run detects.
'   2 REPORT     per provider: is a credential present, WHERE it rests (sbx
'                store / host env / workspace .env), and under which name(s).
'                An env-carried key is reported as a DEPRECATION, not a pass.
'   3 OFFER      the two routes the operator already has, made first-class:
'                  subscription  the agent's own login, run once inside a
'                                sandbox; proveo never sees the token
'                  api key       read on a TTY, never from argv or a file,
'                                written straight to `sbx secret set`
'   4 STORE      under BOTH names while the map exists — the service id the
'                broker path reads and the env var name the forward path and
'                every harness read. This is B2's slug map, built where the
'                operator is already answering questions.
'   5 VERIFY     one authenticated request per provisioned provider, so init
'                answers "spendable", not merely "present" — the distinction
'                the suite reports as `present but the provider does not accept
'                it (HTTP 401)`.
'
' ── THE NAMING SCHEME, DECIDED 2026-09-15 ──────────────────────────────────
' B2 said "map, don't rename" without saying what the map contains. It contains
' two rules, because a store entry has to say WHICH KIND of credential it holds:
'
'   API KEY       the registry's own `provider.Name`. Measured across the 30
'                 registry entries, that IS "env var minus _API_KEY" for 27 of
'                 39 detect vars, so the rule reads the way an operator expects
'                 while the registry stays the single authority. Its six
'                 exceptions are deliberate canonical ids and must not be
'                 re-derived textually:
'                   GEMINI_API_KEY         google      (not gemini)
'                   ZHIPUAI_API_KEY        zai         (not zhipuai)
'                   PERPLEXITYAI_API_KEY   perplexity  VENICEAI_API_KEY  venice
'                   GITHUB_COPILOT_API_KEY copilot     AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY azure
'   SUBSCRIPTION  the DEF name where proveo has one — CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
'                 stores as `claudecode`, beside `anthropic` for the api key.
'                 Where no def owns it, `<service>-sub`: GH_COPILOT_TOKEN →
'                 copilot-sub, HF_TOKEN → huggingface-sub,
'                 AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK → bedrock-sub.
'
' Six detect vars are neither shape — AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and
' GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS among them. B4 already covers these: a provider
' the proxy cannot inject keeps a host-resolvable reference and is never
' brokered, so it needs no slug.
'
' WHY THE KINDS MUST BE DISTINGUISHABLE, measured the day this was decided: a
' subscription was stored as `anthropic` to test the naming hypothesis, and
' TestClaudeCodeAuth/api-key/broker still returned 401 — correctly, because the
' probe authenticates as an API KEY and the proxy was attaching an OAuth token
' into an x-api-key header. One id per provider cannot carry both kinds, and a
' store that hides the difference turns a naming fix into a silent 401.
'
' ── DEPRECATING ENV-CARRIED CREDENTIALS ────────────────────────────────────
' Sequencing matters: removing the env path before init can fill the store
' would leave an operator with no way in.
'
'   P1 ADDITIVE   DONE. init writes the store; env keeps working, unchanged.
'                 An untouched amber field imports on accept, so the migration
'                 costs no retyping. The three steps below are the open ones.
'   P2 PREFERRED  a store entry OUTRANKS the env var of the same provider.
'                 Silent precedence is how an empty stale entry beats a good
'                 env key, so the run header must say which won and why —
'                 sbx-secret-store-is-global is the hazard this must not repeat.
'   P3 WARNED     a run that finds a key only in the workspace .env warns with
'                 the move command; workspace-env-key.puml is the file that
'                 retires here.
'   P4 REFUSED    forward stops accepting a plaintext key for any provider the
'                 proxy can inject. B4 already decided the exception: providers
'                 that CANNOT be injected keep a host-resolvable reference.
'
' Nothing above changes credential-boundary.puml's property. The agent holds
' sentinels either way; this plan changes only where the real value rests
' between runs and who put it there.
'
' ── WHAT IT UNBLOCKS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT ─────────────────────────────────
' Measured against the 2026-09-15 suite, so the claim is countable rather than
' hopeful. Of eleven distinct failures:
'
'   NOT FIXED BY THIS PLAN ALONE   the three broker 401s. Measured: naming is
'                     necessary and insufficient. They need brokering to exist
'                     for mixin-kit defs first; the slug map then lets the
'                     declared credential find its value.
'   ADDRESSED BY STEP 5, WHICH SHIPPED   the chrome-bridge early exit, whose
'                     cause is a login the provider refuses. `verifySlot` now
'                     sends one authenticated request, so init reports the
'                     refusal instead of calling the credential done.
'   NOT CREDENTIALS   the other seven. --local-model never reaching the agent,
'                     subprojects carrying no _spec or git under sbx, the kit
'                     shape, the settings cache. A credential surface fixes
'                     none of them and must not be offered as though it does.
'
' The suite's own rule follows from that split. A test whose credential is
' ABSENT or UNSPENDABLE skips, naming the provider and the init command that
' provisions it. A test whose credential is PROVABLY GOOD — forward returns 200
' — may never skip on a 401: that is the defect, and skipping it is how the
' defect stops being reported.

title OPEN — brokering for mixin kits, then the four-step retirement\nof env-carried credentials; the init surface they need already ships

actor "operator" as OP

node "the host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "proveo init\nreadiness, then credentials" as INIT <<app>>
  database "sbx secret store\nhost-wide, outlives every run" as STORE <<db>>
  database "host env / workspace .env\nthe surfaces being retired" as ENV <<error>>
}

cloud "the provider" as PROV <<cloud>>
component "sbx proxy\nattaches the header" as PROXY <<cloud>>
component "the agent\nsentinels only" as AGENT <<app>>

OP ARROW_MAIN INIT : ""proveo init""
INIT ARROW_QUEUE OP : per provider — present? where? spendable?
OP ARROW_MAIN INIT : subscription login · or a key, read on a TTY
INIT ARROW_MAIN STORE : ""sbx secret set"" under BOTH names
INIT ARROW_QUEUE PROV : verify — one authenticated request
ENV ARROW_ERROR INIT : reported as deprecated, with the move command
STORE ARROW_MAIN PROXY : the value the proxy injects
PROXY ARROW_MAIN PROV : ""Authorization"" attached outside the agent
AGENT ARROW_QUEUE PROXY : sends ""proxy-managed"", holds no key

note bottom of STORE
  **Two names, one secret, until the map lands.**
  proveo writes the env var name and reads the
  service id, so a store holding only
  ""ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"" declares no credential and
  the provider answers 401 to a valid key.
end note

note right of INIT
  **Present is not spendable.**
  The suite already reports a token the provider
  refuses with HTTP 401, so init verifies with one
  real request rather than checking that a name
  exists somewhere on the host.
end note

note bottom of ENV
  **Retire in four steps, never in one.**
  Additive, then preferred, then warned, then
  refused. Removing the env path before init can
  fill the store leaves the operator no way in.
end note

@enduml
